{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1435862-some-questions-re-the-pure-2e","id":1435862,"title":"Some questions RE: The Pure. (2E)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-02-18T10:22:06-08:00","id":1435862,"title":"Some questions RE: The Pure. (2E)","content":"I am working on an idea for a W:tF crossover Chronicle, one where the antagonists are a pack of Pure, and as such I had some questions about them.<br /> <br /> 1: Do the Pure packs regularly incorporate Ghost Wolves into their ranks, wolves who subscribe to general Pure philosophies and have forsworn Luna but don't fit any of the Pure tribes?<br /> <br /> 2: What exactly is the penalty for breaking one of the tribal oaths? AFAICT, it just acts as a Breaking Point towards Flesh. Is there any penalty beyond that?<br /> <br /> 3: Could someone give me a slightly clearer idea of what the Pure tribe oaths actually mean? Or is that supposed to be ambiguous, up to me to figure out exactly how sharply it binds my antagonists?<br /> <br /> Would appreciate feedback on these matters!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26379-aeshdan","name":"Aeshdan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26379_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-18T12:22:45-08:00","id":1435880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aeshdan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1435862-some-questions-re-the-pure-2e#post1435862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am working on an idea for a W:tF crossover Chronicle, one where the antagonists are a pack of Pure, and as such I had some questions about them.<br /> <br /> 1: Do the Pure packs regularly incorporate Ghost Wolves into their ranks, wolves who subscribe to general Pure philosophies and have forsworn Luna but don't fit any of the Pure tribes?<br /> <br /> 2: What exactly is the penalty for breaking one of the tribal oaths? AFAICT, it just acts as a Breaking Point towards Flesh. Is there any penalty beyond that?<br /> <br /> 3: Could someone give me a slightly clearer idea of what the Pure tribe oaths actually mean? Or is that supposed to be ambiguous, up to me to figure out exactly how sharply it binds my antagonists?<br /> <br /> Would appreciate feedback on these matters!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> 1. Pure Ghost Wolves is an interesting idea. I think it's important to remember that the Pure don't have auspices and compensate with more powerful tribes so a Pure Ghost wolf would be missing out on a big piece of the Werewolf template. I imagine they do exist, but if I was building a Pure Ghost Wolf I would probably give them some other source for favoured Gifts, Renown, and Hunters Aspect. Maybe they would have a particularly strong relationship with a personal/pack Totem Spirit and derive more power from that.<br /> <br /> 2. Mechanically this is all that happens, but if you read the section on Oathbringers and page 71 its obvious that there are social consequences as well. Packs are expected to keep their own members in line, and if a pack tolerates flagrant disregard of the Oath they will probably find themselves shunned or even attacked by their neighbours. Furthermore, I would personally rule that egregious breaches of your Tribal Oath can get you ejected from the Tribe - the Firstborn willingly severing their ties to you for your betrayal.<br /> <br /> 3. I'd suggest picking up Shunned by the Moon if you haven't already, chapter one has a great write-up on how Pure characters work - the Tribal Oaths the Pure swear are listed there too. They seem about as open to interpretation as the ones the Forsaken swear. The Fire-Touched and Predator Kings' oaths seem pretty straightforward while the Ivory Claws oath is specifically said to be open to interpretation. The Pure also swear an Oath that functions equivalently to the Oath of the Moon, so it's fair to say they have rules against cannibalism and murdering other Werewolves the same way the Urdaga do","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2384-aurumae","name":"Aurumae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-18T12:54:13-08:00","id":1435881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aeshdan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1435862-some-questions-re-the-pure-2e#post1435862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am working on an idea for a W:tF crossover Chronicle, one where the antagonists are a pack of Pure, and as such I had some questions about them.<br /> <br /> 1: Do the Pure packs regularly incorporate Ghost Wolves into their ranks, wolves who subscribe to general Pure philosophies and have forsworn Luna but don't fit any of the Pure tribes?</div> </div> </div> </div>Regularly? No. But it\u2019s definitely possible if the Ghost Wolf is willing to have their Auspice removed but then forego joining a tribe. The Pure regard Auspice as the major mark of Luna slavery so they\u2019re not going to allow any Ghost Wolf who won\u2019t follow that basic tenet. On the flip side, it would be a very rare Ghost Wolf who would have enough commitment to Pure ideals to undergo the torture of having their Auspice removed, but lacked the conviction to want to join one of the tribes.<br /> <br /> Possibly more common, some Pure packs may tolerate individual Ghost Wolves living in the territory and occupying the outermost fringes of the pack structure - basically expecting them to \u2018wise up\u2019 at some point. They won\u2019t be particularly trusted or let in on pack secrets, but they won\u2019t be driven out or killed. (For a while, at least.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2: What exactly is the penalty for breaking one of the tribal oaths? AFAICT, it just acts as a Breaking Point towards Flesh. Is there any penalty beyond that? </div> </div> </div>Not too much mechanically. Socially, the tribe will expect some kind of penance. Also, the tribal oaths of each of the Pure tribes match up with their sacred prey preferences. Extreme or repeated violations place that character in the valid sacred prey category - some tribal pack is going to hunt them down. (This is a deliberate design consequence.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3: Could someone give me a slightly clearer idea of what the Pure tribe oaths actually mean? Or is that supposed to be ambiguous, up to me to figure out exactly how sharply it binds my antagonists? </div> </div> </div>There\u2019s deliberately some ambiguity. The Pure have more leeway to interpret what their oaths mean to them than the Forsaken have. (Just another proof of moon slavery.) But again, other nearby packs may disagree with the interpretation, and may choose to make an issue of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","user":"Bunyip","date":". 02-18-2021, 03:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-19T06:14:37-08:00","id":1436003,"title":"","content":"Pure ghost wolves could have failed a tribal initiation, I mean, I think those are still a thing, tribal initiations I mean, nothing saying that they have to succeed on that even if they already lost their auspice, sucks for them big time though because they wouldn't have neither tribal nor auspice blessings","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24813-aeveth","name":"Aeveth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-25T13:59:10-08:00","id":1437040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aeveth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1435862-some-questions-re-the-pure-2e?p=1436003#post1436003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pure ghost wolves could have failed a tribal initiation, I mean, I think those are still a thing, tribal initiations I mean, nothing saying that they have to succeed on that even if they already lost their auspice, sucks for them big time though because they wouldn't have neither tribal nor auspice blessings</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think 2e wastes a single paragraph regarding Tribal Initiations - it's a topic covered from A to Z in 1e, but a bit of a blindspot to new players integrating themselves with the newest edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-25T17:28:52-08:00","id":1437061,"title":"","content":"Well, they have to join a tribe someway, joining a tribe isn't automatic, and while the book don't mention initiation rites, they also don't mention any new methods for joining a tribe, though I'm not sure if I remember hints about initiations in the Pack or not, could be thinking about lodges.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24813-aeveth","name":"Aeveth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24813_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-25T22:10:04-08:00","id":1437084,"title":"","content":"Personally, until something that\u2019s 2e says otherwise I assume it\u2019s as simple as swearing the tribe\u2019s vow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}